From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] iio: adc: qcom-spmi-vadc: scale the battery thermistor

LR_MUX1_BAT_THERM had no scaling, so it showed up as a raw voltage and
nothing could read a battery temperature. Downstream msm8974 kernels scale
it with a battery-thermistor table (qcom,scale-function = <1>,
adcmap_btm_threshold2 in qpnp-adc-common.c) that mainline does not carry.
Add that table as SCALE_BATT_THERM and use it for the channel.

An earlier version of this patch used the generic 100k pullup curve. On
the Xperia Z1 Compact that read 40.7C where the downstream table reads
43.3C, and a charger that derates on temperature needs the real figure.

---
--- a/drivers/iio/adc/qcom-vadc-common.c	2026-04-01 20:06:17.000000000 +0400
+++ b/drivers/iio/adc/qcom-vadc-common.c	2026-10-16 12:26:38.656572018 +0400
@@ -100,6 +100,127 @@
 	{ 46,	125000 },
 };
 
